WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.367 --> 00:00:01.834
 Chris.

00:00:01.934 --> 00:00:03.202
Jeremiah.

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:04.671
Congratulations, you've
made it to the final round

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:06.339
of this competition, which
means that you're both one

00:00:06.406 --> 00:00:09.074
step closer to the title
of Forged in Fire Champion

00:00:09.141 --> 00:00:11.511
and a check for $10,000.

00:00:11.611 --> 00:00:13.379
Now we're sending you
back to your home forges

00:00:13.445 --> 00:00:17.116
to recreate an iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:17.182 --> 00:00:23.956
That weapon is-- a pair
of Viking War Axes.

00:00:24.056 --> 00:00:24.957
Good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:25.057 --> 00:00:26.092
We'll see you five days.

00:00:26.159 --> 00:00:29.295 line:14%
[music playing]

00:00:32.464 --> 00:00:35.935
 It feels good to be home, back
out where there's no people.

00:00:36.035 --> 00:00:39.171
I'm not a big people person.

00:00:39.238 --> 00:00:41.707
Today I'm making
two Viking Axes.

00:00:41.774 --> 00:00:44.943
I've made some tomahawks in the
past and some axes in the past.

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:46.780
I use a lot of
low-layer Damascus

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:49.682
so I'm going to do
one 17-layer billet.

00:00:49.748 --> 00:00:54.887
Hopefully out of that I can
get what I need for both axes.

00:00:54.954 --> 00:00:55.921
This is a bigger billet.

00:00:55.988 --> 00:00:58.557
Normally I start
with a 13-layer.

00:00:58.624 --> 00:01:00.960
Lucky me.

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:03.162
To get them both
turned in the eye-form,

00:01:03.262 --> 00:01:05.264
I'm just going to cut
a little 2-inch piece

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:06.766
off an inch and a
half round stock

00:01:06.833 --> 00:01:10.102
and then I can start
turning the eye.

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:13.072
Jeremiah's been bladesmithing
for a few decades

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:14.841
and I've been doing it
for a couple of years.

00:01:14.941 --> 00:01:17.242
So I'm kind of the
underdog so to speak,

00:01:17.309 --> 00:01:21.180
but I love the challenges
that come with that.

00:01:21.246 --> 00:01:23.449
I'll feel good when it's
done and it's right.

00:01:23.516 --> 00:01:26.619
Probably another three
days before I'll feel good.

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:34.460
 I'm excited to get working
on these Viking Axes.

00:01:34.526 --> 00:01:37.030
I'm taking the advantage
of having two forges

00:01:37.130 --> 00:01:41.333
so that hopefully I can
have it done twice as fast.

00:01:41.433 --> 00:01:44.437
If I learned anything from
the first two challenges,

00:01:44.504 --> 00:01:47.206
is that I need to stand on
the shoulders of giants.

00:01:47.306 --> 00:01:49.375
I'm going to stand on
the shoulders of history

00:01:49.442 --> 00:01:52.678
and I'm doing as close
to traditional as I can.

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:55.915
What I'm going to do now is
put this one into the gas

00:01:56.015 --> 00:01:58.651
forge, switch to the
other one out and get

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:00.720
them both to the same spot.

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:04.423
My biggest concern is
that I get them identical.

00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:07.226
Being a blacksmith, people
want things that look

00:02:07.292 --> 00:02:08.560
exactly the same all the time.

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:11.664
So not to say that it's
easy, but it's a challenge

00:02:11.731 --> 00:02:12.899
that I'm prepared for.

00:02:12.965 --> 00:02:15.334 line:14%
They're identical.

00:02:15.401 --> 00:02:18.137 line:8%
I'm pretty happy with
what I got done yesterday.

00:02:18.237 --> 00:02:20.039
Pretty much have all
the forging done.

00:02:20.139 --> 00:02:22.642
I can go on to the heat-treat.

00:02:22.742 --> 00:02:26.245
My biggest concern, just a nice
even heat all the way around.

00:02:26.311 --> 00:02:28.480
The heat-treat is everything.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:30.349
A lot of things can
go wrong-- twist-age,

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:36.222
the warp-age, breakage,
bend-age, --age, whatever.

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:38.757
If it's not heat-treated
then it's just

00:02:38.857 --> 00:02:39.826
a pretty looking wall hanger.

00:02:47.667 --> 00:02:49.101
Yeah, she's straight.

00:02:49.168 --> 00:02:50.570
Time to do it again.

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:58.610
Two for two so far.

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:01.147
It feels good to have the
heat-treat successful.

00:03:01.213 --> 00:03:02.381
I don't know if you
could tell it or not,

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:06.351 line:8%
but I was pretty
nervous, you know.

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:08.154 line:8%
 I'm forge-welding
a high carbon

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:10.522
bit into the body of the axe.

00:03:10.622 --> 00:03:13.092
Making a durable edge
which is historical.

00:03:13.192 --> 00:03:15.895
I'm so nervous, I'm shaking.

00:03:15.962 --> 00:03:19.364
Whenever you do a forge-weld
there's always the chance

00:03:19.464 --> 00:03:20.967
that something could go wrong.

00:03:21.067 --> 00:03:24.770
If the welds fail, I
won't have anything.

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:27.173
[bleep]

00:03:27.239 --> 00:03:29.609
They got way too thin
right up back here,

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:32.811
the seams are showing, the
welds are not going to hold.

00:03:32.878 --> 00:03:35.748
This is the worst thing
that I could have imagined.

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:38.651
I need to start over.

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:40.119
I'm in big trouble.

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:42.388
There's no room for
these emotions right now.

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:44.390
I have a job that
needs to get done.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:47.527 line:8%
I don't quit until
the work is done.

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:50.129 line:8%
 Today is all about
getting the handles fit up.

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:51.997
I'm doing the pressure-fit.

00:03:52.098 --> 00:03:53.800
There's no epoxy,
there's no pens.

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:55.568
It's a purely mechanical fit.

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:58.704
It just slides on in the tap
and locks it into place and--

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:02.174
If the pressure fits not
right any good shock to it

00:04:02.241 --> 00:04:05.544
could drop it down.

00:04:05.611 --> 00:04:06.746
[bleep]

00:04:06.812 --> 00:04:10.582
One of my taxes doesn't
match the other one.

00:04:10.682 --> 00:04:12.885
The bottom's wider than
the top and it needs

00:04:12.985 --> 00:04:14.520
to be tapered the other way.

00:04:14.587 --> 00:04:17.657
So the only choice I have is
to do it from the top down

00:04:17.757 --> 00:04:19.025
and put a wedge in it.

00:04:19.125 --> 00:04:22.095
I guarantee that Jeremiah is
going to do a pressure-fit.

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:23.462
Because that's the way
it's supposed to be,

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:25.397
so I didn't want
to be the guy that

00:04:25.464 --> 00:04:27.600
took the easy way out
and just put a wedge in

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:28.901
and call it good.

00:04:29.001 --> 00:04:31.037
The most annoying thing is
is that it's historically

00:04:31.137 --> 00:04:36.175
not correct and hopefully that's
not what bites me in the ass.

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:38.277
 As you know I'm still
nursing an injury.

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:40.713
To be my arm today I'm
bringing a special guest

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:41.847
from Marcaida Kali.

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:44.183
Please welcome Staff
Sergeant Chris Manz,

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:46.885
today he will be my arm--

00:04:46.985 --> 00:04:49.321
or arms to test your weapons.

00:04:49.422 --> 00:04:50.856
Chris, you're up first.
You ready?

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:51.591
 Let's do it.

00:04:51.658 --> 00:04:54.427
[music playing]

00:05:08.140 --> 00:05:10.710
 All right, Chris, let's talk
about your Viking War Axes.

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:14.213
On the initial cut the long
beard that you have right

00:05:14.313 --> 00:05:16.349
there, hooked all the ribs.

00:05:16.416 --> 00:05:19.551
And of course, the beauty
of having a secondary weapon

00:05:19.651 --> 00:05:23.121
is that when he pulled it
out, he had enough attacks

00:05:23.188 --> 00:05:24.623
to disemboweled everything.

00:05:24.723 --> 00:05:29.361
Overall sir, your Viking
War Axe will kill.

00:05:29.428 --> 00:05:30.496
 Thank you.

00:05:30.596 --> 00:05:32.298
 Jeremiah, shall we do this?

00:05:32.365 --> 00:05:33.265
 Yes, we shall.

00:05:33.366 --> 00:05:36.469
[music playing]

00:05:48.914 --> 00:05:52.785
 All right, Jeremiah,
your Viking Warrior Axes

00:05:52.852 --> 00:05:54.286
are razor sharp.

00:05:54.353 --> 00:05:56.088
It not only blew
through the ribs,

00:05:56.154 --> 00:06:00.126
but dug in breaking through
the lungs and into the heart.

00:06:00.193 --> 00:06:03.762
It is fast and light
and it will kill.

00:06:03.829 --> 00:06:04.897
 Thank you.

00:06:04.964 --> 00:06:06.665
 To test the strength
and overall construction

00:06:06.766 --> 00:06:08.067
of your War Axes,
I'll be throwing

00:06:08.134 --> 00:06:11.037
them three times with
each axe into our mock-up

00:06:11.104 --> 00:06:12.571
of a drawbridge.

00:06:12.638 --> 00:06:16.275
Now hopefully they'll stay
tight and right, not loosen up.

00:06:16.341 --> 00:06:17.042
Chris, you ready?

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:17.810
 Let's do it.

00:06:17.877 --> 00:06:20.847
[music playing]

00:06:39.664 --> 00:06:41.267
 All right, Chris, first off--

00:06:41.334 --> 00:06:43.535
they're balanced nicely
and they match, which is

00:06:43.635 --> 00:06:44.836
really what I was looking for.

00:06:44.903 --> 00:06:47.106
That stout edge though
kind of keeps them

00:06:47.172 --> 00:06:48.707
from penetrating overly deep.

00:06:48.807 --> 00:06:51.243 line:8%
You can see right
about here there's

00:06:51.309 --> 00:06:53.579 line:14%
just a small role in two spots.

00:06:53.679 --> 00:06:56.915
But they're solid,
they're still together.

00:06:56.982 --> 00:06:57.683
Nicely done.

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:58.984
 Thank you.

00:06:59.051 --> 00:07:00.219
 Jeremiah, you're ready?

00:07:00.286 --> 00:07:01.387
 Didn't get
dressed-up for nothing.

00:07:01.454 --> 00:07:04.624
[music playing]

00:07:22.008 --> 00:07:25.411
 So first off, Jeremiah, they
feel like they weigh the same.

00:07:25.511 --> 00:07:27.479
They definitely throw the
same and having that curve

00:07:27.546 --> 00:07:29.348
on the blade, allows
them to dig a lot

00:07:29.448 --> 00:07:30.950
deeper than having a flat edge.

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:35.154
But the bottom-line is neither
of your blades took any damage.

00:07:35.254 --> 00:07:36.221
Well done.

00:07:36.288 --> 00:07:37.823
 Thank you.

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:39.525
 To test the sharpness of your
blades, see how they held up,

00:07:39.592 --> 00:07:41.460
I'm going to take your
axes and deliver it three

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:44.096
shots to these three fish.

00:07:44.197 --> 00:07:45.030
Chris, you're up first.
You ready?

00:07:45.097 --> 00:07:45.865
 Let's do it.

00:07:45.932 --> 00:07:48.935
[music playing]

00:08:04.083 --> 00:08:06.953
 Well, Chris, the gods
of war will be happy.

00:08:07.053 --> 00:08:08.286
There's blood on your axe.

00:08:08.387 --> 00:08:09.722
It's a good day.

00:08:09.789 --> 00:08:11.790
The shape of that blade,
I was a little concerned

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:14.259
just because it's flat,
but it really just

00:08:14.359 --> 00:08:15.427
cut right through those fish.

00:08:15.494 --> 00:08:17.296
Very, very sharp
blades, well done.

00:08:17.363 --> 00:08:18.463
 Thank you, sir.

00:08:18.530 --> 00:08:19.331
 Jeremiah, you're up.

00:08:19.431 --> 00:08:20.031
You ready?

00:08:20.132 --> 00:08:20.900
 Time for sushi.

00:08:20.967 --> 00:08:23.903
[music playing]

00:08:39.384 --> 00:08:41.453
 Well, Jeremiah, same effect.

00:08:41.553 --> 00:08:42.788
Your axes are bloodied.

00:08:42.854 --> 00:08:45.457
They're now honorable
Viking War Axes.

00:08:45.524 --> 00:08:46.725
They are beautiful.

00:08:46.825 --> 00:08:48.127
I like what you did
with the copper inlay.

00:08:48.194 --> 00:08:52.798
I'm not a huge fan in
how thin the handles are.

00:08:52.864 --> 00:08:57.369
To swing it took a little
bit more finger gripping.

00:08:57.436 --> 00:08:59.337
Two very well-made axes.

00:08:59.438 --> 00:09:00.473
Obviously sharp.

00:09:00.573 --> 00:09:01.339
Well done.

00:09:01.406 --> 00:09:03.108
 Thank you.

00:09:03.175 --> 00:09:03.843
 Chris.

00:09:03.943 --> 00:09:04.743
Jeremiah.

00:09:04.810 --> 00:09:06.245
The judges have
examined your work

00:09:06.311 --> 00:09:07.613
and they've tested your weapons.

00:09:07.680 --> 00:09:09.581
They've made their
final decision.

00:09:09.681 --> 00:09:13.218
The Forged in Fire
Champion is Jeremiah.

00:09:13.319 --> 00:09:14.687
Congratulations.

00:09:14.754 --> 00:09:17.722
Chris, your axes did
not make the cut.

00:09:17.822 --> 00:09:19.925
Doug Marcaida will tell you why.

00:09:19.991 --> 00:09:23.628
 Chris, both weapons performed
equally all the way through,

00:09:23.728 --> 00:09:26.432 line:8%
but in the strength
test, one of your axes

00:09:26.498 --> 00:09:28.667 line:8%
took damage on its
edge that made us

00:09:28.733 --> 00:09:30.836
decide that you're going home.

00:09:30.937 --> 00:09:31.971
 I understand.

00:09:32.037 --> 00:09:36.676
 Chris, please
surrender your War Axes.

00:09:36.742 --> 00:09:39.745 line:8%
 Always disappointed if you
don't win, but the experience

00:09:39.845 --> 00:09:42.414 line:8%
that you get from
this competition,

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:44.049
I've loved every minute of it.

00:09:44.116 --> 00:09:46.218
I'm going to go back home
and keep making knives.

00:09:46.285 --> 00:09:48.721
And I'll probably make a
Viking Axe on the side.

00:09:51.557 --> 00:09:52.924
 Jeremiah, congratulations.

00:09:53.024 --> 00:09:54.660
You are our new Forged
in Fire Champion

00:09:54.727 --> 00:09:57.396
and that's a title that comes
with a check for 10 grand.

00:09:57.463 --> 00:09:58.430
How do you feel?

00:09:58.497 --> 00:09:59.431
 That's amazing.

00:09:59.498 --> 00:10:00.632
 You did excellent work.

00:10:00.732 --> 00:10:03.435
Please present your
axes to the judges.

00:10:03.535 --> 00:10:04.436
 I did it.

00:10:04.503 --> 00:10:06.138
I won Forged in Fire.

00:10:06.204 --> 00:10:09.674
To be validated as a smith
this way, is really cool.

00:10:09.741 --> 00:10:11.477
This is a win for my family.

00:10:11.544 --> 00:10:12.744
Certainly a win for
the history books.

00:10:12.811 --> 00:10:16.015
Stay in school, study
your history and it'll

00:10:16.082 --> 00:10:16.548
come in handy.

00:10:16.649 --> 00:10:19.885
[music playing]

